# netsurf: <script type=module> graphs load between frames too
#
# Roadmap WS-C1, second half (patch 159 did import()). A static module
# graph was still fetched (blocking curl) and compiled inside
# js_exec_module when the conversion ran the script: on the Vita ~8 s with
# no frames or input, mostly reading the card.
#
# - macsurf_qjs.c: js_module_prefetch() starts a qjs_modload pipeline (the
#   one import() uses: non-blocking fetch_get_set transfers, compile in
#   12 ms slices) for a module script's static imports as soon as its text
#   is known; js_module_prefetch_pending() says whether one of the realm's
#   is still loading. qjs_modload_new() is shared with qjs_module_defer.
# - script.c: prefetch an external module when its fetch is done (before
#   active drops, so the conversion sees it pending) and an inline module
#   when the parser queues it.
# - html.c: html_can_begin_conversion() holds the conversion (which runs
#   the deferred and module scripts, then DOMContentLoaded) while a
#   prefetch is pending, re-polled every 30 ms, so script and event order
#   is unchanged; js_exec_module then finds the graph compiled and only
#   links and runs it. Every transfer keeps its 120 s timeout, so the hold
#   is bounded (browsers also delay DOMContentLoaded for module graphs).
# - script.c/html.h: inline modules now run in document order WITH the
#   deferred scripts (each remembers how many scripts precede it) instead
#   of after all of them.
# Test: JS-module-static-async.html 5/5 (httpd /slow/ serves one leaf of
# each graph after 1 s). Disarmed (no prefetch): longest timer gap 2035 ms,
# check 3 fails; armed: 17 ms, and both graphs load in parallel (1.2 s
# instead of 2.2 s). Without the order fix check 5 read ext,defer,inl.
diff --git a/content/handlers/html/html.c b/content/handlers/html/html.c
